  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Nastya and Kostya watch from the bar. They discuss Max and Victoria. We'll hear it in Russian first; don't worry about catching every word. Let's listen closely to their conversation in Russian first, and then walk through each line together.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Максим молодец.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Он помог Вике.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Он спас вечер.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, она наговорила гадости.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ему всякие гадости.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И ей очень стыдно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "И как же она это исправит?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Что она будет делать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А, водка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она нальёт ему водки.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Это хороший план.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она знает, что делать.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let's go through it line by line. Kostya nods toward Max.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Максим молодец.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Maxim did great.' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'Maxim' straight to 'well done'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Он помог Вике.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He helped Vika.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'he' with 'Vika'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Он спас вечер.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He saved the evening.' Notice how 'he' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'evening'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, она наговорила гадости.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yeah, she said awful things.' The '-a' ending on the past-tense verb for 'said' shows that the subject is feminine.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ему всякие гадости.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'All sorts of awful things to him.' Notice how 'him' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'nasty things'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И ей очень стыдно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And she feels terrible.' Nastya links 'and' directly with 'to her' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "И как же она это исправит?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'So how's she going to make it right?' Kostya combines 'and' with 'to fix' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Что она будет делать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What will she do?' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'what' with 'do'. Then Nastya responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А, водка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Ah, vodka.' Nastya links 'and' directly with 'vodka' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она нальёт ему водки.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She will pour him vodka.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'it' with 'vodka'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Это хороший план.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'That's a good plan.' Kostya links 'this' directly with 'good' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она знает, что делать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She knows what to do.' The question word for 'what' comes right at the start, followed directly by 'do'. Now let's hear the whole scene once more, start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
